drm/sun4i: set the DE33 global control bit the vendor sets

Every DE33 register that can be compared between a working muOS and this tree
agrees, except two -- and one of those turns out to be a symptom rather than a
cause. This sets the one that is genuinely a configuration difference.

Measured with regmap's debugfs dumps on our side and busybox devmem on the
vendor side, on an anbernic,rg40xx-v with the screen lit:

	                         vendor      ours (before)
	0x1008100 GLOBAL_CTL     0x00000041  0x00000001
	0x1008104 (see below)    0x00000111  0x00000100
	0x1008108 GLOBAL_SIZE    0x01DF027F  matched
	0x100810c GLOBAL_CLK     0x00000001  matched
	0x1281000 BLEND_PIPE_CTL 0x00000101  matched
	0x1281004 BLEND_BKCOLOR  0xFF000000  matched
	0x1281008 BLEND_OUTSIZE  0x01DF027F  matched

GLOBAL_CTL bit 6 is what this patch adds. Its meaning is unknown -- it is set
by the Allwinner BSP on DE33 and not by mainline, and that is the entire
justification. It reads back correctly afterwards.

IT DOES NOT FIX THE DISPLAY. The panel still shows a uniform colour that does
not follow the framebuffer. This is committed because matching a configuration
known to drive this hardware is worth more than not matching it, and because
the measurements are worth keeping.

On 0x1008104, and a dead end worth recording so nobody repeats it: DE2 lays out
the top block as GLOBAL_CTL 0x0, GLOBAL_STATUS 0x4, GLOBAL_DBUFF 0x8,
GLOBAL_SIZE 0xc, while DE33 has GLOBAL_SIZE at 0x8 and GLOBAL_CLK at 0xc. That
made 0x4 look like the new home of the double-buffer commit register, which
matters because sun8i_mixer_commit() does this:

	if (mixer->cfg->de_type != SUN8I_MIXER_DE33)
		regmap_write(engine->regs, SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_DBUFF, ...);

i.e. DE33 never latches its shadow registers at all, which would explain the
symptom exactly. It was tried, from both the commit path and from
sun8i_mixer_init(), and 0x1008104 kept reading 0x00000100 even though
GLOBAL_CTL in the same window took its new value in the same function. A write
that does not stick where a neighbouring write does means the register is not
writable: 0x4 is still GLOBAL_STATUS on DE33, and the vendor's 0x111 against
our 0x100 is the DE reporting that it is running, which ours is not. A symptom.

So DE33's real commit register, if it needs one, is not in the top window, and
upstream's guard may be deliberate rather than an oversight. That question is
still open; see HANDOFF for what has and has not been eliminated.

Upstream status: not upstream, not a backport. Do not send this anywhere until
the display actually works and it is known whether this bit matters.

The diff is generated with diff(1) rather than written by hand, after three
failed attempts at hunk arithmetic.
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.h	2026-08-09 18:25:30.000000000 +0000
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.h	2026-08-12 22:02:07.836529013 +0000
@@ -25,6 +25,12 @@
 #define SUN50I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CLK			0xc
 
 #define SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_RT_EN		BIT(0)
+/*
+ * Set by the vendor BSP on DE33 and not by mainline. Meaning unknown; it is
+ * simply the only other difference in this block against a configuration
+ * known to drive a panel.
+ */
+#define SUN50I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_DE33_EN		BIT(6)
 
 #define SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_DBUFF_ENABLE		BIT(0)
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c	2026-08-09 18:25:30.000000000 +0000
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun8i_mixer.c	2026-08-12 22:02:07.836529013 +0000
@@ -465,8 +465,13 @@
 	}
 
 	/* Enable the mixer */
-	regmap_write(top_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL,
-		     SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_RT_EN);
+	if (mixer->cfg->de_type == SUN8I_MIXER_DE33)
+		regmap_write(top_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL,
+			     SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_RT_EN |
+			     SUN50I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_DE33_EN);
+	else
+		regmap_write(top_regs, SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL,
+			     SUN8I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CTL_RT_EN);
 
 	if (mixer->cfg->de_type == SUN8I_MIXER_DE33)
 		regmap_write(top_regs, SUN50I_MIXER_GLOBAL_CLK, 1);
